Check Docker image
-> docker images

Get JDK / Create container
docker run -dit --name bold_kilby openjdk:22-jdk


2. Copy JAR into container
docker cp target/rest-demo.jar bold_kilby:/tmp/rest-demo.jar

--> docker commit bold_kilby teleusko/rest-demo:v2
    -> we don't want default command . i want to change 

3. Create Docker image
docker commit --change="CMD [\"java\",\"-jar\",\"/tmp/rest-demo.jar\"]" bold_kilby telusko/rest-demo:v2


4. Run the image
docker run -p 8080:8080 telusko/rest-demo:v2

